title: Case Manager › Active cases › Step-down plans from accepted denials
route: /manager
intro: When the clinic accepts a denial in Denial Intelligence, Active cases gets a 'Step-down plan' for it, between 'Being prepared' and the tracker. The card is there only while at least one plan exists. Each plan names the case, the denial it came from and one button that opens the case.
dir: TD
also: Reset demo data clears the plans.
---
start s1 "Denial Intelligence › the clinic accepts a denial"
store st1 "The accepted denial is recorded\nWhich denial (for example D-3318), its request, the payer and the demo-clock time"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Accept the denial"
start s2 "Open Case Manager (Active cases tab)"
decision d1 "Has any denial been accepted?"
process p0 "No card\nActive cases shows 'Being prepared', then the tracker"
screen c1 "Card 'Step-down plans'\n'Started when Denial Intelligence accepts a denial. Choose the next level of care and book the first visit.'\nOne row for each accepted denial, newest first"
screen r1 "A row\nLevel chip ('Residential 3.5')\n'Step-down plan'\nCase ID, 'M.C., 38', payer name\n'From denial D-3318 · accepted 10/20'\nButton 'Open case'"
process p1 "Search, level of care and payer from the filter bar narrow the plans\nThe tracker's status filter does not apply\nWhen nothing matches, the whole card is hidden"
click c2 "Click the case ID or 'Open case'"
process p2 "Go to /authorizations/case/ and the case code of the denial's request (R-0997)"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case"
store st2 "'Reset demo data' clears the plans"
end e1 "Plans are on screen"
end e2 "Active cases as before"

s1 --> st1 --> g1
st1 --> d1
s2 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p0 --> e2
d1 -->|Yes| c1 --> r1 --> p1
r1 --> c2 --> p2 --> g2
p1 --> e1
st1 -.-> st2
